script = ExtResource("1_412ko")
dialogue_id = "mq_4_40_abdication"
record_title = "Era 四: The Avatar's Decision"
text = "PAGE: avatar_adult(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)
avatar_adult: Father, may I speak with you?
scribe: Always, Your Holiness.
scribe: You look well today.
avatar_adult: Thank you, Father.
avatar_adult: I am.
avatar_adult: The old texts...
avatar_adult: I understand the Enlightened One's will now.
scribe: I knew the day would come!
scribe: The legacy of Scribes across the centuries, finally bearing fruit.
scribe: Tell me, Your Holiness, what must we do?
avatar_adult: Before that, I want to thank you.
avatar_adult: You have raised me with warmth, and wisdom.
avatar_adult: You gave me a home when I was just a child from a distant shard.
scribe: It has been the greatest honor of my life.
avatar_adult: Well... let me quote to you the sacred words of the Enlightened One.
avatar_adult: \"To force the ten thousand things into one is to destroy them.\"
scribe: I understand.
scribe: We must not use force.
scribe: We must gain the people's favor through the debate.
avatar_adult: No...
avatar_adult: I am going about this the wrong way.
avatar_adult: Father, I know the Enlightened One's will now.
avatar_adult: And in my heart, I know the world will not be made better if everyone follows me.
scribe: What?
scribe: But the debate is going so well!
scribe: The people are ready to follow you!
avatar_adult: Father, please...
scribe: It is my failing.
scribe: I pushed you too hard.
scribe: I placed the burden of the world on you before the spirit was ready.
avatar_adult: You did nothing wrong.
avatar_adult: You raised me to care for our people, and that is exactly why I must leave them.
avatar_adult: To stay would be to build an empire.
avatar_adult: An empire that will burn people like wood.
avatar_adult: I want to offer warmth, but burn no wood.
scribe: But the Enlightened One commanded us to put the shards back together!
scribe: That commandment has been handed down from Scribe to Scribe from the day of the Shattering.
avatar_adult: Yes, but...
avatar_adult: I hear the words of the Enlightened One.
avatar_adult: \"A fine bowl holds water even if cracked.\"
avatar_adult: Our world is a cracked bowl, true.
avatar_adult: And the cracks are big.
avatar_adult: But it's a fine, well-crafted bowl.
avatar_adult: It can hold water despite the cracks.
scribe: So the Enlightened One truly wants us to leave these shards scattered?
avatar_adult: We still have the gates.
avatar_adult: We can still be whole in spirit.
scribe: ...
scribe: I am the Scribe of the Enlightened One.
scribe: A Scribe's duty is to transmit the commandments.
scribe: If it is the Enlightened One's will, then it is not my place to object.
avatar_adult: Father, there will be no more commandments from the Enlightened One.
avatar_adult: I am leaving the Haven to walk my own path.
avatar_adult: But the people will still need your wisdom."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
